{"id": "EUVD-2026-86200", "enisaUuid": "412abef0-7cc8-3483-814f-2244bf119098", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix sd_ndr.data memory leak in ksmbd_vfs_set_sd_xattr\n\nndr_encode_v4_ntacl() allocates sd_ndr.data via kzalloc() at entry.\nIf any subsequent ndr_write_*() call returns error during encoding,\nthe allocated sd_ndr.data won't be freed and causes memory leak.\n\nMove kfree(sd_ndr.data) into out label to ensure the buffer gets\nreleased on all success and error return paths.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/306d6f370da7e0e5532dc51c972f4ce101e42431", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc55270e410ccb4d24e637c13b5c4c25bcd106d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c866c3314a6853eb06c7a8bef67f43c8a8bdfb6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b4dec75498fd0a1c9eaea680aef59c9519eb16f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c521dd78e036b5e0cfd394dd2ff2218890dd9e41", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4d56b00c7df88cd5751e7415bdfabc9fdbc82a7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7f3p-w572-qm2q", "CVE-2026-93812"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a29c5b3-ad09-312d-8d5b-d4d67a1848bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1b3e3572-031e-36e2-833f-40787e69b161", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "22838cf3-a3f6-3bd8-a6d8-fc3470971310", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "303fff2b8c77a85c62dbde3b27c24b084144c04c <9b4dec75498fd0a1c9eaea680aef59c9519eb16f"}, {"id": "5e511bd7-4b77-39f9-b13c-eb24f70ec5a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "303fff2b8c77a85c62dbde3b27c24b084144c04c <dc55270e410ccb4d24e637c13b5c4c25bcd106d7"}, {"id": "6cf70c8a-faf4-33eb-862a-87289221e0c2", "product": {"name